<div style="border: 2px solid #1a5276; padding: 15px; text-align: center; background-color: #e0f2f7;">
    <h1 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # In Ten Years, I Will... – Lesson # 3</h1>
    <p style="color: #1a5276; font-size: 1.1em; margin: 5px 0 0 0;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 3</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Speaking</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 10th Grade (CEFR: B1.1)</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Future Plans and Time Capsule</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> In Ten Years, I Will...</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Speaking: Productive: Explain how to use common technological devices and applications. Interactive: Exchange opinions about the results of surveys and investigations.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Speaking: Can explain to classmates how to use a device to record goals for a time capsule (e.g., "Press this button to start recording."). Can exchange ideas about future goals and skills for career planning (e.g., "I think critical thinking will be important for my career."). Can discuss future career trends by sharing survey results and personal views related to Panama (e.g., "According to our class survey, many students want to pursue careers in tourism and eco-friendly innovation, which reflects Panama's focus on environmental conservation.").</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f0f8ff; color: #1a5276;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f0f8ff; color: #1a5276;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f0f8ff; color: #1a5276;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher starts by showing images of various time capsules or future-oriented objects (e.g., a drone, a virtual reality headset, sustainable energy devices, a digital tablet with a recording app open). Students are asked to share what they see and what these items *might* be used for in the future. The teacher prompts with "Imagine it's 2034. What will people be using this for?" This activates vocabulary related to technology, future, and possibilities, building on previous lessons. Students briefly discuss in pairs what they think will be important in ten years.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models how to express future goals using modals and future continuous, relating it to a device. For example, holding up a smartphone: "In ten years, I *might* be using this device to teach virtual classes from my home. I *will be working* as an online educator. I believe students *will be learning* through interactive AI platforms." The teacher emphasizes the pronunciation of the long /iː/ sound in words like 'achieve' and 'engineering' and practices stress in 'critical thinking' and 'problem-solving' as students repeat examples.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
                <ul style="margin-top: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"If I say 'I *might* pursue a career in technology,' am I 100% sure?" (Expected answer: No, it's a possibility.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What does 'I *will be working* as a software developer' mean? Is it happening now, or will it be an ongoing action in the future?" (Expected answer: It will be an ongoing action in the future.)</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Teacher provides examples using target vocabulary: "Many students *will be studying* engineering" (future continuous). "I *might* consider an internship" (modal for possibility).</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">5-7 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Future Plans and Time Capsule".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short audio recording (or teacher-read dialogue) of two Panamanian teenagers discussing their future plans for a class time capsule project, including advice they received and some initial survey results. The genre is an informal dialogue, register is semi-formal/conversational, and format is audio/transcript. It incorporates vocabulary like 'career', 'goals', 'skills', 'critical thinking', 'data analyst', 'engineering', 'tourism', 'eco-friendly innovation', and phrases like "I might pursue...", "I will be working...", "My teacher said that I should...".</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Speaking: Exchange opinions about the results of surveys and investigations.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b> Students listen to the audio twice.</p>
                <ul style="margin-top: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist question:</b> "What are the two teenagers mainly talking about?" (Expected answer: Their future plans and careers for a time capsule, and advice they got.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False:</b> Students check statements based on the dialogue (e.g., "One student wants to be a data analyst. T/F", "Their teacher recommended pursuing only traditional careers. T/F").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Information Matching:</b> Match the career goal (e.g., 'software developer') with the skill mentioned (e.g., 'problem-solving') from the dialogue.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">8-10 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Speaking.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Using modals for career possibilities (might, could), future continuous for ongoing plans (will be working/studying), and reported speech to share advice (said that I should/could). Target vocabulary: career, future, goals, possibilities, advice, education, technology, engineering, software developer, data analyst, skills, leadership, problem-solving, critical thinking, community service, pursue, accomplish, reflect, suggest, recommend, develop, enhance, explore, volunteer, consider, gain.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul style="margin-top: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Controlled Practice: Sentence Completion & Oral Read-Aloud (5 min):</b> The teacher provides sentence stems on the board or a handout, focusing on the target grammar. Students complete them orally in pairs. Example stems: "In ten years, I _______ (be working) as a ______ because I think _______ (critical thinking) will be important." "My parents _______ (say) that I ______ (should consider) a career in _______." "I _______ (might pursue) a degree in _______." Students then read their completed sentences aloud to their partner, focusing on accurate pronunciation of /iː/ and word stress in 'leadership,' 'problem-solving,' etc.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Semi-Controlled Practice: Advice Chain (5 min):</b> Students sit in a circle. The first student states a future goal or a skill they want to develop (e.g., "I want to enhance my problem-solving skills for a career in engineering."). The next student then shares advice they *might* give, or *could* give, using reported speech (e.g., "My friend said that I *should volunteer* for community service to develop leadership skills."). They continue around the circle, building on previous statements. The teacher monitors for correct grammar and vocabulary use.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Pair Interaction: Future Outlook Interview (7 min):</b> Students work in pairs. Partner A interviews Partner B about their future goals for the time capsule using question prompts like: "What would you like to achieve in five years?" "What skills do you think you *will be developing* in your chosen career?" "What advice have you received about your future, and who said it?" (e.g., "My uncle said that I *should explore* possibilities in renewable energy."). Students use the target grammar and vocabulary. They swap roles after 3-4 minutes. Teacher circulates, providing feedback on fluency, grammar, and pronunciation.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">17 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Future Plans and Time Capsule".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Students will engage in a "Future Career Fair & Time Capsule Item Explanation" simulation. They will work in small groups (3-4 students) to discuss their individual future plans, incorporating survey results from previous lessons (e.g., "According to our class survey, many students want to pursue careers in tourism and eco-friendly innovation, which reflects Panama's focus on environmental conservation."). Each student then presents an item they would put into a hypothetical time capsule to represent their future goals and explains its significance to their group members, acting as if they are "exhibiting" at a career fair.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Group Discussion and Individual Explanation/Presentation.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul style="margin-top: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students are divided into small groups.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Within each group, they first conduct a brief "survey results discussion." One student acts as a "recorder" to note key points. They discuss career trends in Panama (e.g., "I think more people *will be pursuing* careers in technology and sustainable development in Panama."), using information from previous lessons and personal views. They exchange opinions, asking "What *do you think* about the idea of working in data analysis?" or "Do you believe tourism *will be growing* significantly in Panama?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Then, each student takes turns. They hold up a chosen item (either a real object they brought, a picture, or a drawing) that represents a future goal for a time capsule. For example, a student might show a drawing of a solar panel and say: "I am including a drawing of a solar panel because it represents my goal to pursue a career in engineering, specifically in renewable energy. In ten years, I *will be working* as a renewable energy engineer. My science teacher said that I *should gain* practical experience now."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">They must explain its connection to their 'In Ten Years, I Will...' statement, using modals for possibilities, future continuous, and reported speech. They must also explain how they *might use* a device to record these goals, (e.g., "I will press this button on my phone to record my voice message for the capsule, explaining my vision for a more sustainable Panama.").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Group members actively listen and ask follow-up questions about the goals and the item choices (e.g., "Why did you choose that item?", "What kind of training *might* you need for that career?").</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">The teacher circulates, monitoring for fluent use of target language, interaction, and task completion, intervening only to facilitate communication if necessary.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">12-15 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy and student self-reflection.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher Observation Checklist. The teacher uses a checklist to note students' use of target grammar (modals, future continuous, reported speech), key vocabulary (career, goals, skills, critical thinking, pursue, accomplish), and the ability to explain device usage and exchange opinions during the group activity.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students participate in the "Future Career Fair & Time Capsule Item Explanation" group discussion and individual explanation. Their performance is assessed based on their ability to articulate their future plans and reasoning.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria:</b></p>
                <ul style="margin-top: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Intelligible pronunciation:</b> Clear pronunciation of words, including the long /iː/ sound and correct stress in multisyllabic words.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Use of target vocabulary:</b> Appropriately uses at least 5-7 key vocabulary words related to careers and future plans.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Clarity and Cohesion:</b> Explains ideas clearly, using modals for possibility, future continuous, and reported speech.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Collaborative Interaction:</b> Actively listens and responds to peers' questions and opinions, exchanging ideas effectively.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Task Completion:</b> Successfully explains item choice and discusses future goals in relation to Panama's context.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete an exit ticket with the following prompts:</p>
                <ul style="margin-top: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"One new idea I learned about future careers in Panama today is..."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"I feel confident/okay/not confident using future continuous to talk about my ongoing plans because..."</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">5-7 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Student and teacher reflection and connection to next lesson.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Reflection:</b></p>
                <ul style="margin-top: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What part of today's speaking activity did I find most challenging, and why?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How can I improve my ability to exchange opinions about future career trends?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher Reflection:</b></p>
                <ul style="margin-top: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What worked well in this speaking-focused lesson? (e.g., student engagement in the role-play, successful use of modals).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What adjustments or scaffolds are needed for students who struggled with forming the future continuous or using reported speech? (e.g., more sentence frames, focused mini-drills, clearer visual aids for grammar structures).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Did students successfully explain device usage for recording goals? Was their pronunciation of key sounds and stress adequate?</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> This lesson focused on speaking about future plans and expressing opinions. The next lesson (Lesson 4: Writing Composition) will build on these ideas by having students write a paragraph or short essay about their chosen career path for the time capsule, incorporating the grammar and vocabulary practiced today, specifically focusing on expressing their future goals and the skills they aim to develop.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">3-5 min</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>